# Design — S-PROBE: extraction feasibility spike (falsify SAEOS-1 §9/A8)

## 1. Purpose and falsification target

The goal is a **spike**, not a build. Its job is to *try to break* the claim that the SAEOS-1
knowledge graph can be reconstructed from artifacts that are **already sealed**, before anyone
spends build effort on it.

**Falsification target (FT).** SAEOS-1 §9 / A8 assert (paraphrase — see `ASM-1`, the verbatim text
is not readable from this stage) that the §4.3 node types can be populated by extraction from the
sealed record, with no new instrumentation at seal time.

**The probe refutes FT if** hand-extraction of three real sealed goals loses too much of the
required field surface, per the pre-registered predicate in §9.

A spike that cannot fail is not a spike. Every rule below is written to bias *toward* refutation:
conservative tie-breaks (§8.3), an adversary pass that may only downgrade (§7.3), and thresholds
frozen before any data is seen (§7.1).

